  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan is a little disappointed after taking Ba Shi Ba’s Immortal Gu. He had expected Ba Shi Ba’s rank eight rule path Immortal Gu to be consecutive Gu, because Ba Shi Ba specialized in the consecutive hit method, but the Gu is addition Gu instead.",
        "chapters": [
          1791
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_ba_shi_ba",
          "sys_immortal_gu",
          "gu_addition_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Consecutive Gu is more famous than addition Gu and more practical in many situations. With rank eight consecutive Gu, Fang Yuan could link many different killer moves to achieve the effect of a consecutive move. A consecutive move links two or more killer moves together for greater power, and normally only elites among Gu Immortals can use that technique.",
        "chapters": [
          1791
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Using consecutive Gu, one can link killer moves of various paths. Fang Yuan names combinations such as myriad ghost sword dragon with great thief ghost hand, or jade flow pearl with strength path giant hand, as the kind of cross-path linking that would raise battle strength sharply.",
        "chapters": [
          1791
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
